The second stage of the L1 reader, written in L1. It takes the tokens from tokenize.prog and builds the syntax tree that the Luau reader builds. A node is [kind [line payload]]: kind 0 is an integer, 1 a symbol, 2 a list (payload: its items), 3 a pair (payload: its items), and 4 a string (payload: its bytes).
The result is [0 node] for a program that parses, and [1 message] for one that does not. A bracket that is not closed, a closing bracket with nothing open, an empty program, and text after the expression are refused this way. A stage never raises: bind passes a success on and a failure through.
---

---
(fn ts
  (let bind (fn (r f) (if (= (head r) 0) (f (tail r)) r))
  (letrec rev
    (fn (l acc) (if (? l) acc (rev (tail l) [(head l) acc])))
  (mutual ((readNode
             (fn ts
               (if (? ts) [1 "the program ends before an expression is complete"]
                   (let t (head ts)
                     (let k (head t)
                       (let line (head (tail t))
                         (let p (tail (tail t))
                           (if (= k 0)
                               (bind (readItems (tail ts) 1 ~)
                                     (fn r [0 [[2 line (head r)] (tail r)]]))
                               (if (= k 2)
                                   (bind (readItems (tail ts) 3 ~)
                                         (fn r [0 [[3 line (head r)] (tail r)]]))
                                   (if (= k 1) [1 "unexpected )"]
                                       (if (= k 3) [1 "unexpected ]"]
                                           (if (= k 4) [0 [[0 line p] (tail ts)]]
                                               (if (= k 5) [0 [[1 line p] (tail ts)]]
                                                   [0 [[4 line p] (tail ts)]])))))))))))))
           (readItems
             (fn (ts closer acc)
               (if (? ts) [1 "a group is never closed"]
                   (if (= (head (head ts)) closer)
                       [0 [(rev acc ~) (tail ts)]]
                       (bind (readNode ts)
                             (fn r (readItems (tail r) closer [(head r) acc]))))))))
    (if (? ts) [1 "the program is empty"]
        (bind (readNode ts)
              (fn r (if (? (tail r)) [0 (head r)]
                        [1 "there is more text after the expression"]))))))))
---
(list [4 1 1]) => [0 [0 1 1]] fuel 100000
(list [0 1 ~] [5 1 "a"] [1 1 ~]) => [0 [2 1 (list [1 1 "a"])]] fuel 100000
(list [0 1 ~] [1 1 ~]) => [0 [2 1 ~]] fuel 100000
(list [2 1 ~] [4 1 1] [4 1 2] [3 1 ~]) => [0 [3 1 (list [0 1 1] [0 1 2])]] fuel 100000
(list [6 1 "hi"]) => [0 [4 1 "hi"]] fuel 100000
(list [5 1 "x"]) => [0 [1 1 "x"]] fuel 100000
(list [0 1 ~] [5 1 "a"]) => [1 "a group is never closed"] fuel 100000
(list [4 1 1] [4 1 2]) => [1 "there is more text after the expression"] fuel 100000
(list [1 1 ~]) => [1 "unexpected )"] fuel 100000
(list [0 1 ~] [3 1 ~]) => [1 "unexpected ]"] fuel 100000
~ => [1 "the program is empty"] fuel 100000
